  "title": "The nine groups of English words",
  "lesson": {
    "kind": "intro",
    "focusPoint": null,
    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Point 1: Review of the last class",
        "body": "What did you learn in the last class?\n\nYou already know many English words. Words are like hikers in a team. Today we climb Mount Ávila with them."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "heading": "Point 2: Every word has a job",
        "body": "On Mount Ávila, do all hikers do the same job? Do all English words?\n\nNo, each hiker has a different job. English words are a team too: 8 parts of speech (clases de palabras) plus the articles a, an, the."
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "heading": "Point 3: Name, act and replace",
        "body": "“Sofia climbs. She sees the mountain.” Which words name, act or replace?\n\nA noun (sustantivo) names: Sofia. A verb (verbo) shows action: climbs. A pronoun (pronombre) replaces a noun."
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "heading": "Point 4: Describe",
        "body": "Mount Ávila has a high peak. Which words say which one and what it is like?\n\n“The” is an article (a, an, the). “High” is an adjective (adjetivo): it says what the peak is like. “Slowly” is an adverb: how we climb."
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "heading": "Point 5: Join and feel",
        "body": "“Sofia climbs with Luis and says: Wow!” What do “with”, “and” and “Wow!” do?\n\n“And” is a conjunction: it joins ideas. “With” is a preposition: it links words. “Wow!” is an interjection: a feeling."
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "heading": "Point 6: Nine groups",
        "body": "The team reached the top. How many groups of words are in the team?\n\nNoun, pronoun, verb, adjective, adverb, preposition, conjunction, interjection, and the articles a, an, the: 9 groups."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "English has 8 parts of speech plus a, an and the: 9 groups. Like hikers on Mount Ávila, each one has its own job.",
    "memoryPhrase": "Noun, pronoun, verb, adjective, adverb, preposition, conjunction, interjection, and the articles a, an, the: 9 groups.",
    "layout": "letter-grid-v2",
